title: '[pallet-revive] add log index field to call tracer output'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    ## Summary

    Adds a monotonic `index` field to `CallLog` in the call tracer output, matching Geth v1.17.0+ behavior ([go-ethereum#33629](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/pull/33629)).

    The `index` represents the transaction-level log index (matching `logIndex` in receipts), distinct from the existing `position` field which tracks ordering relative to subcalls within the same trace frame.

    Closes https://github.com/paritytech/contract-issues/issues/277

    Companion PR: https://github.com/paritytech/evm-test-suite/pull/145

    ## Changes

    - `CallLog`: new `index: u32` field with hex serialization
    - `CallTracer`: new `log_count` counter incremented on each `log_event` call
    - `ReviveApi` bumped to `api_version(2)`. `trace_block`, `trace_tx`, and `trace_call` keep their
      v1 signatures via `#[changed_in(2)]` so new nodes can still decode trace responses from
      pre-bump runtimes. Legacy wire shapes (`TraceV1`, `CallTraceV1`, `CallLogV1`) are added in
      `evm::api::debug_rpc_types` alongside `From`-based downgrade conversions.
    - Updated `call_tracing_works` test to verify correct monotonic indices across nested call depths

    ## Test plan

    - [x] All 9 tracing tests pass
    - [ ] evm-test-suite snapshots need regenerating against Geth v1.17.0 (companion PR: paritytech/evm-test-suite#TBD)
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
